{
 "esm": "1.2.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "GWDOBlockingDrag",
  "description": "The low-level flow-blocking drag, and the total stress profile the momentum stage differentiates. Lines 553-592 of `phys/physics_mmm/bl_gwdo.F90` (WRF 4.8, NCAR/MMM-physics CCPP kernel `bl_gwdo_run`).\n\nAir that cannot carry itself over the sub-grid ridge goes AROUND it instead of over it, and the form drag of that deflection is a separate stress from the gravity wave. The scheme decides how deep the blocked layer is by an energy argument: descending from the top of the search, it compares the kinetic energy of the flow at each level against the potential energy it would have to spend to be lifted to the height of the highest sub-grid peak,\n\n    PE(z) = integral from z to the top of the search of N^2(z') (z_komax - z') dz'\n    KE(z) = (u^2 + v^2)/2\n\nand the blocking top is the HIGHEST level at or below the peak where PE has caught up with KE. The potential energy is a genuine cumulative column integral -- the Fortran spells it `bnv2*(zl(komax)-zl)*del/g/rho`, in which `del/g/rho` is nothing but the hydrostatic layer thickness -- so it is written here as `integral(..., var: lev, lower: lev_nodes, ...)` and lowered by the EarthSciDiscretizations `integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top` rule, with the consumer-supplied measure `dz` bound to that thickness. Its value at interface k is exactly the Fortran's accumulator at layer k, so the interface field is read at the layer index.\n\nThe stress itself is a bulk form drag, 0.5 rhobar (coefm/area) Cd dxyp olp zblk U^2 with Cd = max(2 - 1/od, 0), applied at the surface and RAMPED LINEARLY TO ZERO at the blocking top. The Fortran writes that ramp as a subtraction recurrence, taufb(k) = taufb(k-1) - taufb(1)/(kblk-1); it is written here in the closed form taufb(1) (1 - (k-1)/(kblk-1)) it is equivalent to, because nothing about it is sequential -- the increment is a constant, not a function of the previous answer -- and esm-spec 4.3.1.1 recurrences are reserved for sweeps that genuinely are. The two differ only by the round-off the repeated subtraction accumulates, about 1e-15 of the surface value over the ten or so layers a blocked column has.\n\nThe component's output is the TOTAL interface stress, the wave stress plus the blocking stress, which is what the Fortran leaves in `taup` and what the tendency is the divergence of.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "wrf",
   "gravity-wave-drag",
   "gwdo",
   "flow-blocking",
   "form-drag",
   "column"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "Choi, H.-J., and S.-Y. Hong (2015). An updated subgrid orographic parameterization for global atmospheric forecast models. J. Geophys. Res. Atmos. 120, 12445-12457.",
    "doi": "10.1002/2015JD024230"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Kim, Y.-J., and J. D. Doyle (2005). Extension of an orographic-drag parametrization scheme to incorporate orographic anisotropy and flow blocking. Quart. J. Roy. Meteor. Soc. 131, 1893-1921.",
    "doi": "10.1256/qj.04.160"
   },
   {
    "citation": "Hong, S.-Y., and co-authors (2025). Revision of the orographic gravity wave drag parameterization in the KIAPS Integrated Model. Wea. Forecasting."
   },
   {
    "citation": "NCAR/MMM-physics bl_gwdo.F90 at commit 52cfbd7 (WRF 4.8 phys/physics_mmm submodule)."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 50,
   "description": "Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound at the mount edge and passed down to the imported grid, to the cumulative-integral rule and to the `sat` subsystem."
  }
 },
 "models": {
  "GWDOBlockingDrag": {
   "expression_template_imports": [
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/grid.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    },
    {
     "ref": "${ESD_ROOT}/grids/column_nonuniform_1d/rules/integral_lev_nodes_cumulative_to_top.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   ],
   "subsystems": {
    "wrf": {
     "ref": "../../../lib/wrf_constants.esm"
    },
    "par": {
     "ref": "./gwdo_parameters.esm"
    },
    "sat": {
     "ref": "./wave_saturation.esm",
     "bindings": {
      "NLEV": "NLEV"
     }
    }
   },
   "variables": {
    "ldrag": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "The column's off switch, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "on": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "1 - ldrag: the arithmetic form of the Fortran's `if (.not. ldrag)` guard around the whole blocking block."
    },
    "komax": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Level index one above the lowest level reaching the maximum sub-grid peak; the blocked air would have to be lifted to THIS level's height, and the blocking top can be no higher."
    },
    "kbomax": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Level index one above the lowest level reaching ELVMAX + 2 var: the top of the downward search, where the potential-energy integral starts from zero."
    },
    "zl": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer-centre heights above sea level, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "bnv2": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Squared Brunt-Vaisala frequency, read from the mounted column state. NOTE that this is the profile whose level-1 entry the column stage replaced with the low-level pressure-weighted mean; the blocking search reads it from kgwdmin = 2 upward, so it never sees the substituted value."
    },
    "rho": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "kg/m^3",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Air density, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "del": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Layer pressure thickness, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "u1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Earth-relative zonal wind, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "v1": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Earth-relative meridional wind, read from the mounted column state."
    },
    "dz": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "GEOMETRIC layer thickness del/(g rho), the hydrostatic thickness the Fortran writes inline as `del(i,k)/g_/rho(i,k)`. It is the measure of the potential-energy integral below, supplied under the bare name every rule of the column_nonuniform_1d grid reads (esm-spec 9.7.7 permits a consumer to supply its own monotone layer measure). It is NOT the measure the column stage uses: that one integrates in mass, because the stress divergence is taken with respect to pressure, and this one integrates in height, because a potential energy is g times a height."
    },
    "pe_dens": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Integrand of the potential-energy integral, N^2 (z_komax - z), zeroed outside the search window [kgwdmin, kbomax] so that the whole-column integral operator reproduces the Fortran's bounded accumulation. Bound to its own layer-shaped observed because the ESD integral rules match a bare field, not a compound."
    },
    "fbdpe_nodes": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Cumulative potential energy per unit mass from each interface to the top of the column grid, integral(pe_dens, var: lev, lower: lev_nodes, upper: z_top). The Fortran's accumulation stops at the top of the search window (zl(komax)); that bound is carried by pe_dens, which is zero outside [kgwdmin, kbomax], so integrating to the grid top is the same sum. (Until 2026-11-11 the upper bound was spelled zl[NLEV], a layer centre; the EarthSciDiscretizations rule never read it and always summed to the grid top, and ESD #39 made the bound the ground name z_top, which says what the lowering does.)"
    },
    "fbdpe": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "The Fortran's `fbdpe` accumulator at layer k: the potential energy the flow at layer k would have to spend to reach the height of the highest sub-grid peak. It is the interface field above read at the BOTTOM face of layer k, which is exactly what a downward accumulation that has just added layer k holds."
    },
    "fbdke": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m^2/s^2",
     "shape": [
      "lev"
     ],
     "description": "Kinetic energy per unit mass of the earth-relative flow at layer k, (u^2 + v^2)/2."
    },
    "kblk": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Top of the blocked layer: the highest level index at or below komax, and within the search window, at which the potential energy has caught up with the kinetic energy; 0 when no level does, or when the column produces no drag. The Fortran finds it by a downward scan that stops at the first hit, which is the same thing as the maximum over the levels that satisfy the test, so it is an aggregate and not a sweep."
    },
    "zblk": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "m",
     "description": "Depth of the blocked layer, the height of the blocking top above the lowest model level."
    },
    "fbdcd": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "1",
     "description": "Bulk form-drag coefficient of the blocked flow, max(2 - 1/od, 0): it vanishes for an obstacle at most half as wide as it is long and saturates at 2 for a very wide one."
    },
    "taufb_sfc": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "description": "Flow-blocking stress at the surface, 0.5 rhobar (coefm/area) Cd dxyp olp zblk U^2, in the Fortran's own left-to-right association."
    },
    "taufb": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "Flow-blocking stress profile: taufb_sfc at the surface, falling linearly to zero at the blocking top, and zero above it."
    },
    "taup": {
     "type": "unknown",
     "units": "Pa",
     "shape": [
      "lev_nodes"
     ],
     "description": "TOTAL interface stress, the saturating wave stress plus the flow-blocking stress. This is what the Fortran leaves in `taup` and what the momentum stage differentiates."
    }
   },
   "equations": [
    {
     "lhs": "ldrag",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.ldrag"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "on",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "-",
      "args": [
       1.0,
       "ldrag"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "komax",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.komax"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "kbomax",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.kbomax"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "zl",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.zl"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "bnv2",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.bnv2"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "rho",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.rho"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "del",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.del"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "u1",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.u1"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "v1",
     "rhs": "sat.oro.col.v1"
    },
    {
     "lhs": "dz",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [
         "del",
         "wrf.g"
        ]
       },
       "rho"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "pe_dens",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "bnv2",
       "zl"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">=",
           "args": [
            "k",
            "par.kgwdmin"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "<=",
           "args": [
            "k",
            "kbomax"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "bnv2",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "zl",
              "komax"
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "index",
             "args": [
              "zl",
              "k"
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        0.0
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fbdpe_nodes",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "integral",
      "args": [
       "pe_dens"
      ],
      "var": "lev",
      "lower": "lev_nodes",
      "upper": "z_top"
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fbdpe",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "k"
      ],
      "args": [
       "fbdpe_nodes"
      ],
      "ranges": {
       "k": {
        "from": "lev"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "fbdpe_nodes",
        "k"
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fbdke",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       0.5,
       {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "u1",
           2
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "^",
          "args": [
           "v1",
           2
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "kblk",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "on",
       {
        "op": "faq",
        "output_idx": [],
        "reduce": "max",
        "args": [
         "fbdpe",
         "fbdke"
        ],
        "ranges": {
         "k": {
          "from": "lev"
         }
        },
        "expr": {
         "op": "ifelse",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": "and",
           "args": [
            {
             "op": "and",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": ">=",
               "args": [
                "k",
                "par.kgwdmin"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "<=",
               "args": [
                "k",
                "kbomax"
               ]
              }
             ]
            },
            {
             "op": "and",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "<=",
               "args": [
                "k",
                "komax"
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": ">=",
               "args": [
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "fbdpe",
                  "k"
                 ]
                },
                {
                 "op": "index",
                 "args": [
                  "fbdke",
                  "k"
                 ]
                }
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          },
          "k",
          0.0
         ]
        }
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "zblk",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "ifelse",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": ">",
        "args": [
         "kblk",
         0.0
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "index",
          "args": [
           "zl",
           {
            "op": "max",
            "args": [
             "kblk",
             1.0
            ]
           }
          ]
         },
         {
          "op": "index",
          "args": [
           "zl",
           1
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       0.0
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "fbdcd",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "max",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         2.0,
         {
          "op": "/",
          "args": [
           1.0,
           "sat.oro.od"
          ]
         }
        ]
       },
       0.0
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "taufb_sfc",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "*",
          "args": [
           {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
             {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
               {
                "op": "/",
                "args": [
                 {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                   {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                     0.5,
                     "sat.oro.col.rhobar"
                    ]
                   },
                   "sat.oro.coefm"
                  ]
                 },
                 "sat.oro.area"
                ]
               },
               "fbdcd"
              ]
             },
             "sat.oro.dxyp"
            ]
           },
           "sat.oro.olp"
          ]
         },
         "zblk"
        ]
       },
       {
        "op": "^",
        "args": [
         "sat.oro.col.ulow",
         2
        ]
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "taufb",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "faq",
      "output_idx": [
       "m"
      ],
      "args": [],
      "ranges": {
       "m": {
        "from": "lev_nodes"
       }
      },
      "expr": {
       "op": "ifelse",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "and",
         "args": [
          {
           "op": ">",
           "args": [
            "kblk",
            0.0
           ]
          },
          {
           "op": "<=",
           "args": [
            "m",
            "kblk"
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "op": "*",
         "args": [
          "taufb_sfc",
          {
           "op": "-",
           "args": [
            1.0,
            {
             "op": "/",
             "args": [
              {
               "op": "-",
               "args": [
                "m",
                1.0
               ]
              },
              {
               "op": "-",
               "args": [
                "kblk",
                1.0
               ]
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        0.0
       ]
      }
     }
    },
    {
     "lhs": "taup",
     "rhs": {
      "op": "+",
      "args": [
